        "title": "What are the possible side effects?",
        "text": "HERNEXEOS may cause severe and life-threatening liver problems and lung problems. It can also cause severe heart problems that may affect your heart’s ability to pump blood, and harm to unborn babies.\n\nThe most common side effects of HERNEXEOS include diarrhea, liver problems, rash, feeling tired, and nausea.\n\nThe most common severe abnormal blood tests include decreased white blood cell count and increased liver function tests."
