        "title": "What are the benefits of this drug?",
        "text": "In the TRUST-I trial, 90% of the 103 patients with ROS1 -positive NSCLC who were ROS1 inhibitor naïve experienced complete or partial shrinkage of their tumors; 72% of these patients had complete or partial shrinkage of their tumors which lasted more than twelve months. In the TRUST-II trial, 85% of the 54 patients with ROS1 -positive NSCLC who were ROS1 inhibitor naïve experienced complete or partial shrinkage of their tumors; 63% of these patients had complete or partial shrinkage of their tumors which lasted more than twelve months.\n\nIn the TRUST-I trial, 52% of the 66 patients with ROS1 -positive NSCLC who were pretreated with an ROS1 inhibitor experienced complete or partial shrinkage of their tumors which lasted more than six months for 74% of patients. In the TRUST-II trial, 62% of the 47 patients with ROS1 -positive NSCLC who were pretreated with an ROS1 inhibitor experienced complete or partial shrinkage of their tumors which lasted more than six months for 83% of patients."
